      "writtenOn": "2023-09-12T05:10:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As of this CL, identity is just a public key, however, in the 3rd CL on this stack, I expand the definition of identity. So in the final version, the signature is verified by the public key in the leaf of `DiceChainEntry` if there is one or more `DiceChainEntry`, otherwise, it is verified with `DiceCertChainInitialPayload`. The latter is applicable to the parties who do not have/cannot present a DICE chain (e.g. remote device).\n\nI will add this clarifications in this CL and the next CL.",
      "parentUuid": "814c0be2_ec6f5458",
      "revId": "e1b88a4e2ed36b3f4a294982359f7253c88b9776",
